OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34102
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FGiving evidence at Derby Crown Court
OL,7,Fon Wednesday, Elliott told jurors he
OL,8,Fheard "screaming and mayhem in the
OL,9,Fbackground" when he was called to help
OL,10,Fofficers detain Mr Green at the police
OL,11,Fstation on the afternoon of December
OL,12,F30, 2022.
OL,14,FThe court heard Mr Green, who has been
OL,15,Fdiagnosed with autism, cerebral palsy
OL,16,Fand asthma, went to the police station
OL,17,Fvoluntarily because he received a
OL,18,Fletter he wanted help with, before an
OL,19,Fofficer decided he needed to be
OL,20,Farrested based on information on the
OL,21,Fpolice computer.
OL,26,@pD@GOUqD@KO]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G2/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34103
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FJurors heard Elliott was not told why
OL,7,FMr Green, who was shouting and ended
OL,8,Fup on the floor, was being arrested.
OL,10,FAsked by defence barrister Adam King
OL,11,Fwhether he felt angry or annoyed by Mr
OL,12,FGreen when he arrived at the police
OL,13,Fstation, Elliott said: "Not in any
OL,14,Fway, shape or form."
OL,16,FThe defendant added: "He was being
OL,17,Floud and noisy but he wasn't being
OL,18,Fthreatening or trying to hurt anyone
OL,19,Fat this point."
OL,26,@uD@XOUvD@TO]xD@VOU{D@OO]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G3/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34104
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FMr Green was handcuffed, carried into
OL,7,Fa police van by officers before
OL,8,Fbanging his head against the floor and
OL,9,Fignoring the defendant's commands for
OL,10,Fhim to "behave", the court heard.
OL,12,FAsked what his priority was, Elliott
OL,13,Fsaid: "(The) safety of my colleagues,
OL,14,Fsafety of myself and the safety of
OL,15,FKian.
OL,17,F"We have a duty of care to him and we
OL,18,Fdon't want him to hurt himself."
OL,26,@rD@HOUrD@OO]uD@GOUyD@AOUzD@`O]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G4/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34105
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FElliott told jurors he thought at the
OL,7,Ftime that Mr Green's "manic behaviour"
OL,8,Fcould have been caused by alcohol,
OL,9,Fdrugs or his mental health.
OL,11,FMr King asked: "When he (Mr Green)
OL,12,Fsaid 'go on Taser me, I'll get you
OL,13,Fdone for it', did that induce any
OL,14,Femotional state in you?"
OL,16,FThe defendant, of Ashbourne in
OL,17,FDerbyshire, replied: "No, it's just
OL,18,Fhim venting his anger or whatever."
OL,26,@oD@VOUoD@fO]sD@POUvD@XO]yD@VOUzD@cO]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G5/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34106
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FThe court heard that in the police
OL,7,Fvan, Elliott struck Mr Green on the
OL,8,Fforehead with his extendable baton,
OL,9,Fcausing blood to run down his face.
OL,11,FElliott said he believed Mr Green was
OL,12,Fgoing to bite his colleague Pc Neil
OL,13,FPalmer, who was searching him, because
OL,14,Fhe grabbed hold of the officer's hand.
OL,16,FAsked by Mr King if he wanted to teach
OL,17,FMr Green a lesson, Elliott replied:
OL,18,F"Absolutely not. My sole aim with the
OL,19,Fstrike was to neutralise the threat
OL,20,Fand get Neil's hand free.
OL,26,@zD@AOU
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G6/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34107
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,F"Unfortunately, the only target area
OL,7,Fwas to the forehead."
OL,9,FHe added: "My lawful purpose was to
OL,10,Fstop the attack that was ongoing on
OL,11,FNeil by Mr Green. Ultimately, I
OL,12,Fsucceeded ` I got control and (got)
OL,13,Fhim to safety."
OL,15,FJurors were shown body-worn camera
OL,16,Ffootage which is said to show Elliott
OL,17,Frolling his eyes.
OL,26,@nD@AOUoD@UO]qD@KOUuD@OO]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G7/9
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,342,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34108
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F341A1785946756
OL,3,CPolice officer denies being angry
OL,4,Cbefore hitting autistic man with baton
OL,6,FThe defendant said he was "not at all"
OL,7,Ffrustrated, telling the jury: "It was
OL,8,Ffreezing cold, Kian's not co-
OL,9,Foperating, we're searching him in the
OL,10,Fback of the van.
OL,12,F"It's not under control. I don't know
OL,13,Fwhat the expression was of the officer
OL,14,Fin the van ` I was possibly
OL,15,Fcommunicating."
OL,17,FThe former constable, who worked for
OL,18,Fthe police for another three-and-a-
OL,19,Fhalf years after the incident in non-
OL,20,Fpublic facing duties, denies assault.
OL,21,FHe has since retired, the court heard.
OL,26,@nD@[OUnD@fO]oD@_OUtD@AOUwD@OO]
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G8/9
